    pr_ref:  # 8bbb
    description: "Detect orphaned tracker-sync PRs at the end of a successful `auto-pr` invocation, so a sync PR that was created mid-cycle but never picked up cannot sit unmerged for hours.\n\n**Motivating incident (session_retrospective_04262026_1911.md Finding 4 / 1736.md timeline 00:33):** During the 2026-04-25→26 session, a tracker auto-sync PR (#3376) was created during a feature PR's auto-pr cycle, CI passed cleanly, but auto-pr exited after merging the feature PR without polling for #3376's merge. The sync PR sat open for ~3 hours until the user noticed (\"pr 3376 is unmerged why the fuck is it unmerged\"). Tracker state on origin was behind the agent's local view, which would have caused conflicts on the next mutation.\n\n**Identification rule (no labels needed):** tracker-sync PRs have a deterministic shape from `packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker/sync.py`:\n- Branch prefix: `tracker-sync/<timestamp>` (sync.py:854).\n- PR title prefix: `tracker: sync N file(s)` (sync.py:963).\n\n**Implementation:**\n\n1. **New helper in `scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh`** (governance file):\n   ```\n   find_open_tracker_sync_prs()\n     api_get \"$API_BASE/pulls?state=open&sort=recentupdate\"\n     filter client-side (Python json shim, mirroring find_merged_pr at :238) for\n       items where head.ref starts with \"tracker-sync/\"\n     emit (PR_NUM, BRANCH, AGE_SECONDS) tuples on stdout\n   ```\n   Reuses existing `api_get` / `FORGEJO_TOKEN` / failover plumbing — no new auth, no new vendor dep, no `gh` dependency.\n\n2. **Wire into `scripts/auto-pr` post-success path** (governance file): immediately after the feature PR's \"Verified: PR was successfully merged\" line, call the helper. For any returned tuple whose AGE_SECONDS is greater than the feature PR's creation-time-to-merge-time delta (i.e., the orphan was already alive when this auto-pr started), emit a vociferous warning:\n   ```\n   ⚠️  Orphaned tracker-sync PR detected:\n        PR #<N> (branch tracker-sync/<ts>, <Xm><Ys> old)\n      Run: ./scripts/merge-pr <N> --wait-for-ci\n      (This PR was open before this auto-pr started — it should have merged\n       on its own auto-sync cycle but appears stuck.)\n   ```\n   Does NOT auto-merge — the warning surfaces the case for human/agent attention. Auto-merging another PR inside auto-pr would conflate two PR lifecycles and break the \"one auto-pr invocation = one PR\" mental model.\n\n3. **Don't warn on freshly-created sync PRs.** If the orphan's age is less than the feature PR's lifetime, it was created during this auto-pr cycle and the next auto-sync threshold-cross will pick it up. The warning is specifically for sync PRs that existed before this cycle and are still open after — the #3376 shape.\n\n**Why post-success path on auto-pr** (vs. stop-hook cooldown):\n- Auto-pr is the natural place: every feature merge passes through it, and it already has FORGEJO_TOKEN loaded and API_BASE resolved.\n- Stop-hook cooldown would also catch this but is vendor-specific (per-vendor hook directories) and only fires when the agent stops; an active session might miss orphans for hours.\n- Wiring at auto-pr post-success means every successful merge is also a \"did anything else slip through?\" checkpoint.\n\n**Governance:** `scripts/auto-pr` and `scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh` are both in the AGENTS.md governance file list. Stays `needs_human_review` pending human approval of the warning shape and threshold logic. Pairs naturally with INV-rahib's auto-pr Scenario B fix (same files, same review cycle).\n\n**Tests:**\n- Unit: `find_open_tracker_sync_prs` against a mocked API_RESPONSE returning a mix of feature-branch and tracker-sync PRs.\n- Integration / property: a fixture session where a tracker-sync PR exists older than the feature PR's start emits the warning; one created mid-cycle does not.\n\n**Cross-references:**\n- session_retrospective_04262026_1911.md Finding 4 (motivating incident).\n- INV-rahib (sibling auto-pr correctness work, same governance batch).\n- `packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker/sync.py` lines 854 + 963 (branch/title prefixes).\n- `scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh` lines 180-210 (`find_open_pr` reference impl) and 227-276 (`find_merged_pr` Python json shim pattern to mirror)."  # 8bbb
